@startuml UC-26 Comment on Blog Post - Sequence Diagram (stereo)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280

actor "Teacher or Moderator" as User
participant ":BlogCommunityPage" as UI <<user interaction>>
participant ":BlogController" as CTL <<coordinator>>
participant ":BlogCommentService" as SVC <<business logic>>
participant ":BlogPostRepository" as POSTS <<interface>>
participant ":BlogCommentRepository" as COMMENTS <<interface>>
database DB

autonumber
activate User
User ->> UI : Enter the comment text in the comment box of the Blog Post Detail screen
activate UI
User ->> UI : Click "Post"
UI ->> UI : addComment()
UI ->> CTL : POST /api/blog-posts/{id}/comments
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : create(postId, content, parentCommentId)
activate SVC
SVC ->> POSTS : findPublishedById(postId)
activate POSTS
POSTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_posts WHERE id = ? AND status = 'PUBLISHED'
activate DB
DB -->> POSTS : row / none
deactivate DB
POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
deactivate POSTS
SVC ->> SVC : sanitize the comment HTML and check that it is not empty and stays within 200 words

alt the blog post no longer exists or is no longer published
  SVC -->> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 404
  UI -->> User : Show that the blog post is unavailable and keep the entered text

else the comment text is empty or exceeds 200 words
  SVC -->> CTL : IllegalArgumentException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 400
  UI -->> User : Highlight the comment box, show MSG02 and keep the entered text

else the comment cannot be saved
  UI -->> User : Show MSG25 and keep the entered comment text

else the post is published and the comment text is valid
  SVC ->> COMMENTS : save(new comment on the post)
  activate COMMENTS
  COMMENTS ->> DB : INSERT INTO blog_comments with post_id = ? and parent_comment_id NULL
  activate DB
  DB -->> COMMENTS : Saved
  deactivate DB
  COMMENTS -->> SVC : BlogComment
  deactivate COMMENTS
  SVC ->> SVC : build the comment view with the author display name and timestamps
  SVC -->> CTL : BlogCommentView
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 201 + BlogCommentView
  UI ->> UI : loadDetail(id)
  UI -->> User : Show MSG08 and the new comment with its author name and time in the discussion
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
deactivate User
@enduml
